      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-62614",
      ":question/problem": "Samuel counted the number of phone calls that his company received each day over the past week. The results are given below:\n\n$55, 24, 29, 31, 45, 12, 5$\n\nWhat is the missing number in the frequency table below?\n\n| Number of Calls | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1 - 20$ | $2$ |\n| $21 - 40$ | $0$ |\n| $41 - 60$ | $2$ |"
