      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-63232",
      ":question/problem": "Margaret, a marketing advisor, counted the number of cakes sold by a bakery each Friday over a certain period. The results are given below:\n\n$13, 4, 15, 3, 12, 7, 17$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing numbers in the frequency table below?\n\n| Number of Cakes | Frequency |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $1 - 5$ | $2$ |\n| $6 - 10$ | $0$ |\n| $11 - 15$ | $0$ |\n| $16 - 20$ | $1$ |"
